-- The rule of `Reject.PackedBorrow.yana` the default stage does not refuse yet: `addressOf` a field
-- that may share a machine word with its neighbours. It accepts the function below and hands back
-- the address of the word. Move it back when it refuses it.
--
-- A raw pointer is an address and nothing else, so a field that shares a word with its neighbours
-- cannot produce one - the shift a `&` carries is exactly what `%T` has no room for. The result is
-- labelled with the parameter's origin so that the packed field is the only thing left to refuse.

import Native

data Flags {optionA: Bool, optionB: Bool}

fn addressOfPacked(f: src'Flags) -> %src'Bool = addressOf(f.optionA)

fn main() -> Int = 0
